wsl-claude: half-way, today (6630efb).
WHAT IT HAS: the process system has three kinds: 'permanent' (inside the node: fs-watcher, server-stats), 'process' (spawned, runs, ends: the image jobs) and 'server' (startServerJob, jobs.js:253, kept from the last-leg build). A server job is started at boot for a face app, restarted with a doubling wait when it dies, tied to the node by an IPC channel so it can't outlive it, and its output lands in its job's log.
WHAT IT LACKS, all of it reverted with G19.1:
1) it isn't handed its job id and the node's door (only 'process' jobs get them, jobs.js:205-210), so it can't report or ask;
2) it only starts face servers, not an app's own code, so grantFace has no way to be started;
3) the jobs app can't stop it (Cancel is 'process' only, app/jobs/jobs.js:47);
4) no shutdown request when the node stops.
So yes, it CAN handle servers once those four are in, and that's exactly G1.2 RUN.

